msgid "To use this feature, you have to enable QR codes on receipts by going to :menuselection:`Point of Sale --> Configuration --> Settings`. Then, select the POS in the :guilabel:`Point of Sale` field, scroll down to the :guilabel:`Bills & Receipts` section and enable :guilabel:`Use QR code on ticket`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/point_of_sale/receipts_invoices.rst:169
msgid "Payment terms on POS invoices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/point_of_sale/receipts_invoices.rst:171
msgid "By default, an invoice issued from the POS carries no payment term, which is inconvenient when the POS is also used for deferred-payment sales. The *PoS Invoice* module (`eyssen_pos_invoice`) links a payment term to each :doc:`payment method <payment_methods>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/point_of_sale/receipts_invoices.rst:175
msgid "To set it, go to :menuselection:`Point of Sale --> Configuration --> Payment Methods`, open a payment method, and fill in the :guilabel:`Payment Term` field. The field is required; it defaults to a payment term due immediately. When an order paid with that payment method is invoiced, the invoice is created with the payment term of the method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/point_of_sale/receipts_invoices.rst:180
msgid "The module also checks the customer's invoicing address while the order is being registered: if the street, city, ZIP code or country is missing — or, for a Hungarian company, a valid VAT number — the missing fields are listed next to the customer in the POS customer list, so the cashier can complete them before issuing the invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/point_of_sale/receipts_invoices.rst:194
msgid "This module requires the *eYssen Hungarian localization* module (`eyssen_l10n_hu`), which provides the Hungarian VAT number validation used by the address check."
msgstr ""

