#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:3
msgid "Blanket orders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:5
msgid "A **blanket order** is a framework agreement: the customer commits to a total quantity of one or more products at an agreed price, and calls that quantity off over time in several ordinary sales orders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:9
msgid "The *Sale Blanket Orders* module (``sale_blanket_order``) adds two menus under :menuselection:`Sales app --> Orders`: :guilabel:`Blanket Orders` and :guilabel:`Blanket Order Lines`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:14
msgid "Create a blanket order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:16
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Sales app --> Orders --> Blanket Orders` and click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:18
msgid ":guilabel:`Partner`: the customer who commits to the quantities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:19
msgid ":guilabel:`Validity Date`: the day the agreement expires. After it, the blanket order becomes :guilabel:`Expired` and no more sales orders can be called off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:21
msgid ":guilabel:`Pricelist`, :guilabel:`Payment Terms`, :guilabel:`Fiscal Position`, :guilabel:`Salesperson`, :guilabel:`Sales Team`, :guilabel:`Customer Reference` and :guilabel:`Tags`: as on a sales order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:24
msgid ":guilabel:`Order Lines`: one line per product, with the :guilabel:`Original Qty` committed, the :guilabel:`Price`, the taxes and an optional :guilabel:`Scheduled Date`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:27
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Confirm` to move the agreement from :guilabel:`Draft` to :guilabel:`Open`. The totals (:guilabel:`Untaxed Amount`, :guilabel:`Taxes`, :guilabel:`Total`) are computed like on a sales order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:40
msgid "Quantity tracking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:42
msgid "Each blanket order line tracks five quantities, so it is always visible how much of the commitment is left:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:45
msgid ":guilabel:`Original Qty`: the committed quantity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:46
msgid ":guilabel:`Ordered Qty`: already called off on sales orders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:47
msgid ":guilabel:`Delivered Qty` and :guilabel:`Invoiced Qty`: the progress of those sales orders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:48
msgid ":guilabel:`Remaining Qty`: what may still be called off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:50
msgid "A blanket order becomes :guilabel:`Done` when nothing remains, and :guilabel:`Expired` when the validity date passes with a remainder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:53
msgid "The :menuselection:`Sales app --> Orders --> Blanket Order Lines` list shows the lines of every blanket order together, which is the quickest way to see what is still open across customers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:57
msgid "Call off a sales order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:59
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Create Sale Order` on the blanket order (or select lines in the :guilabel:`Blanket Order Lines` list and use the same action). In the pop-up, enter the :guilabel:`Quantity to Order` for each line — the :guilabel:`Remaining quantity` is shown next to it — and click :guilabel:`Create and View Order`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:64
msgid "The generated sales order takes the blanket order's price, taxes, payment terms and pricelist, and each of its lines keeps a :guilabel:`Blanket Order line` link. Confirming that sales order increases the :guilabel:`Ordered Qty` of the blanket order line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:76
msgid "The :guilabel:`Sale Orders` smart button on the blanket order opens every order called off from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:79
msgid "Restricting the called-off orders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:81
msgid "By default a salesperson can still add other products to an order created from a blanket order. To prevent that, enable :guilabel:`Disable adding more lines to SOs` in :menuselection:`Sales app --> Configuration --> Settings`. Orders that originate from a blanket order then only accept the lines that came from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/blanket_orders.rst:87
msgid "The :guilabel:`Blanket Orders` menu is visible to sales administrators; salespeople see the :guilabel:`Blanket Order Lines` list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:3
msgid "Commissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:5
msgid "Commissions reward salespeople for the business they bring in. The **Commissions** module records a commission for every customer invoice line that matches a rule, so the amount paid out is derived from actual invoicing — not from a manual estimate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:9
msgid "A commission is always the result of three records:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:11
msgid "a **commission plan**, which defines the period the commissions belong to;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:12
msgid "one or more **commission rules** inside that plan, which decide *which* invoice lines earn a commission and *how much*;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:14
msgid "the **commissions** themselves, one per invoice line and rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:19
msgid "Install the **Commissions** module from the :menuselection:`Apps` application. Installing it also installs :guilabel:`Margins` (``sale_margin``), because margin-based rules read the deal margin from the sales order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:23
msgid "The module adds two access rights, under the :guilabel:`Commissions` category of the user form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:25
msgid ":guilabel:`User`: sees their own commissions only. Every salesperson gets this level automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:27
msgid ":guilabel:`Administrator`: sees every commission, and is the only level that can create plans and rules, collect and recompute commissions, and change a frozen deal salesperson. Sales administrators get this level automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:31
msgid "Accounting users also see every commission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:43
msgid "Commission plans"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:45
msgid "To create a plan, go to :menuselection:`Sales app --> Configuration --> Commissions --> Plans` and click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:48
msgid ":guilabel:`Name`: a label for the period or the scheme, for example `Sales 2026`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:49
msgid ":guilabel:`Date From` / :guilabel:`Date To`: the invoice dates the plan covers. Both are optional; leaving one empty makes that side unbounded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:51
msgid ":guilabel:`Company`: the company the plan belongs to (only shown in a multi-company database). A plan never collects commissions from another company's invoices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:54
msgid "Rules are added in the :guilabel:`Rules` tab. The plan's dates, company and rules can only be changed while the plan is in the :guilabel:`Draft` stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:69
msgid "Plan stages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:71
msgid "A plan moves through three stages, using the buttons in the header:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:73
msgid ":guilabel:`Draft`: the plan is being prepared. Click :guilabel:`Start` to activate it. At least one active rule is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:75
msgid ":guilabel:`Running`: the plan collects commissions. Posted customer invoices whose invoice date falls inside the plan's period are matched against the plan's rules automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:77
msgid ":guilabel:`Closed`: the plan no longer collects anything. Click :guilabel:`Reset to Draft` to reopen it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:80
msgid "Two more buttons are available while a plan is :guilabel:`Running`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:82
msgid ":guilabel:`Collect`: scans every posted customer invoice, credit note and receipt in the plan's period and creates the commissions that are still missing. Use it after adding a rule to an already running plan, or after posting invoices while the plan was still in draft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:85
msgid ":guilabel:`Recompute`: rebuilds the rate and amount of the commissions already collected, from the current rules and the current sales order margin. Collected commissions are otherwise frozen, so later cost changes cannot move them; use :guilabel:`Recompute` after changing a rule's bands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:89
msgid "The :guilabel:`Commissions` smart button on the plan opens the commissions collected by it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:92
msgid "Commission rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:94
msgid "A rule answers two questions: which invoice lines it applies to, and how much they earn. Rules are added from the :guilabel:`Rules` tab of a plan, or from :menuselection:`Sales app --> Configuration --> Commissions --> Rules`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:98
msgid "Within one plan the rules are evaluated in the order of the list (drag the handle to reorder), and **the first matching rule wins** — an invoice line never earns twice from the same plan. Put the most specific rules at the top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:103
msgid "When to pay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:105
msgid "The :guilabel:`Trigger` field decides when a collected commission becomes payable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:107
msgid ":guilabel:`Invoice Posted`: as soon as the invoice is posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/commissions.rst:108
msgid ":guilabel:`Invoice Paid` (default): only once the invoice is fully paid. Invoices that are only *in payment* do not count."
