#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:23
msgid "skips periods that ended before :guilabel:`Billing Resumes On`, so a paused subscription is not billed retroactively;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:25
msgid "adds an invoice line carrying the billed period, and applies the contract's :guilabel:`Coupon`, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:28
msgid "Lines of the same contract are billed onto **one** invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:31
msgid "One run catches up at most 24 missed periods per line. This is a guard: a mis-set :guilabel:`Start Date` would otherwise generate years of history in a single run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:35
msgid "Draft or posted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:37
msgid "The contract's :guilabel:`Invoice Posting` policy decides what happens to the generated invoice:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:39
msgid ":guilabel:`Leave as draft for review` (default): the invoice stays in draft, for an accountant to check and post."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:41
msgid ":guilabel:`Post automatically`: the invoice is posted immediately, and — if the contract has a :guilabel:`Payment Token` — an :doc:`automatic charge <automatic_payments>` is attempted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:44
msgid ":guilabel:`Paid Until` only moves forward on **posted** invoices, so a draft invoice never makes the line look billed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:48
msgid "The generated invoice"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:50
msgid "The invoice is an ordinary customer invoice in the contract's :guilabel:`Billing Journal`. It is flagged as a subscription invoice and links back to the subscription lines it bills; each invoice line stores the :guilabel:`Period Start` and :guilabel:`Period End` it covers. The line label comes from the line's :guilabel:`Invoice Note` when one is set, with `#START#`, `#END#` and `#PERIOD#` replaced by the billed period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:65
msgid "Changing a running subscription"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/subscriptions/billing.rst:67
msgid "Changes to a running line are recorded in its :guilabel:`Change History` tab with the old and the new value, so the reason for a changed invoice amount can always be traced. Changes take effect from the next period that is billed; already posted invoices are not modified."
msgstr ""

