#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:6
msgid "Right of withdrawal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:8
msgid "The **Right of withdrawal** feature lets a webshop consumer formally *withdraw from the contract* — the legally binding, no-reason cancellation guaranteed to consumers by EU law — directly from the customer portal, without contacting support and without logging in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:12
msgid "It is built on top of the standard eYssen **RMA** (Return Merchandise Authorization) system: the :doc:`backend <withdrawal/backend>` adds a dedicated, non-rejectable *withdrawal declaration* record, while the :doc:`customer portal <withdrawal/consumer_portal>` adds the public, two-step declaration flow and the durable-medium confirmation e-mail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:18
msgid "End-to-end flow (summary)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:20
msgid "**Consumer** opens the declaration from the order page or from the order e-mail link (:doc:`withdrawal/consumer_portal`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:22
msgid "They choose **product** quantities (shipping lines are never offered), confirm, and receive a durable-medium confirmation e-mail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:24
msgid "A **withdrawal declaration** is created in the backend already in :guilabel:`Posted` state under :menuselection:`Sales --> Orders --> Withdrawals`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:26
msgid "When goods come back, the **agent** clicks :guilabel:`Start Return / Refund` → works a normal RMA (Post → accept lines → Done → validate receipt → credit note). See :doc:`withdrawal/backend`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:31
msgid "Legal background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:33
msgid "The feature implements the mandatory online **withdrawal button** required by **Directive (EU) 2023/2673** (which amends the Consumer Rights Directive 2011/83/EU, articles 11a and 11b). For distance and off-premises contracts, the trader must offer consumers an easily accessible electronic withdrawal function and confirm receipt of the withdrawal on a **durable medium** (e.g. e-mail)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:40
msgid "The on-screen legal wording (button labels, the declaration text and the confirmation e-mail) is provided as a **draft pending legal review**. Have the texts approved by your legal counsel before going live. The texts live in editable QWeb templates and a :guilabel:`mail.template`, so they can be adjusted without code changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:46
msgid "Key principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:48
msgid "The withdrawal declaration is treated very differently from an ordinary return request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:50
msgid "**Legally binding and irrevocable.** A confirmed withdrawal can never be *rejected* — it is a unilateral consumer statement. The backend enforces this with database-level guards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:52
msgid "**Immutable proof.** At confirmation time the system stores a frozen snapshot of the declaration (consumer, products, quantities, exact timestamp) and sends a durable-medium confirmation e-mail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:54
msgid "**No automatic logistics.** A withdrawal never auto-generates a return picking or a refund. An RMA agent decides how to handle the physical return and the refund manually via :guilabel:`Start Return / Refund` (see :doc:`withdrawal/backend`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:57
msgid "**Stays Posted.** A confirmed declaration remains in :guilabel:`Posted` forever. That is normal — it is *not* stuck. The physical return and refund run on a **separate ordinary RMA**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:59
msgid "**Goods only.** Carrier shipping lines (``is_delivery``) cannot be withdrawn or returned as standalone items. Only product lines appear on the portal form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/withdrawal.rst:61
msgid "**B2C scope only.** The feature is available only for genuine business-to-consumer webshop orders (see :doc:`withdrawal/consumer_portal`)."
msgstr ""

